<Layout title="About" description="Learn about Data Savvy Solutions and Steven Jenkins’s practical approach to business intelligence, reporting, and data automation.">
  <div class="shell"><header class="page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">About Data Savvy Solutions</p><h1>Data should make<br />work clearer.</h1><p class="lede">A practical approach to business intelligence: understand the question, make the numbers useful, and help people act with confidence.</p></header>
  <section class="detail-row" aria-labelledby="steven"><div><p class="number">THE PERSON BEHIND THE WORK</p><h2 id="steven">Hi, I’m Steven Jenkins.</h2></div><div><p>I’m building Data Savvy Solutions around business intelligence, useful reporting, and thoughtful data workflows. My focus is on turning complex information into something people can understand and use.</p><p class="mt-5">Working with tools such as Tableau, SQL, and Python, I approach a project by looking at the business question first. The goal is a solution that fits the work, with clear definitions and a handoff that makes sense.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="principles"><p class="eyebrow">How I approach the work</p><h2 class="mb-10" id="principles">Useful by design.</h2><div class="service-grid"><article class="service-card"><p class="number">01 /</p><h3>Clarity before complexity</h3><p>Start with the question and build only what helps answer it.</p></article><article class="service-card"><p class="number">02 /</p><h3>Definitions before dashboards</h3><p>Make sure everyone understands what a number means and where it comes from.</p></article><article class="service-card"><p class="number">03 /</p><h3>Understanding that lasts</h3><p>Document the logic and the workflow so the solution stays useful after handoff.</p></article></div></section>
  <section class="pb-20" aria-label="Connect with Steven"><ContactCTA /></section></div>
</Layout>
